Package: clustGLMM
Title: Model-Based Clustering of Mixed-Type Longitudinal Data
Version: 1.0
Encoding: UTF-8
Authors@R: c(person("Jan", "Vavra", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                    email = "vavraj@karlin.mff.cuni.cz"))
Description: Provides an MCMC sampler for modelling multivariate regression models 
  for numeric, count, binary, ordinal and count outcomes observed repeatedly on the same units. 
  Possible relations among outcomes are captured through joint distribution of random effects.
  Moreover, different clusters of different nature are found through model-based clustering principles.
  These clusters are defined through cluster-specific parameters, choice of which is up to the analyst.
  The most useful declaration of cluster differences is through the regression setting,
  where model formula can be tailored specificaly for each outcome. It consists of four parts
  1. fixed - regression coefficients common to all clusters,
  2. group - group-specific regression coefficients,
  3. random - random effects specific for each unit,
  4. offset - name of an offset variable (if needed).
  MCMC sampler consists of Gibbs and Metropolis-Hastings steps. 
  The sampled chains can be monitored by wide variety of plotting functions.
  Post-processing requires checks for label-switching.
  Final units clustering can be done quickly based on sampled allocation indicators
  or by proper exploration of posterior distribution of classification probabilities.
License: GPL-2
Imports: coda, colorspace, gaussquad, graphics, grDevices, HDInterval, MASS, methods, mvtnorm, nnet, splines, stats, utils